column1:
Note: df: degrees of freedom; 
H: statistic of Kruskal-Wallis test; 
F: F-statistic;
R²: coefficient of determination;
P-values < 0.05 are considered statistically significant.
Alpha Diversity: Statistical significance of differences among groups was evaluated using the Kruskal-Wallis H test (or Wilcoxon rank-sum test for pairwise comparisons).The table presents the test statistics and P-values for diversity indices (e.g., Shannon, Chao1).
Beta Diversity: Analyses were performed based on the Bray-Curtis dissimilarity matrix.PERMANOVA (Permutational Multivariate Analysis of Variance) was used to test for significant differences in community composition among groups (999 permutations).
PERMDISP (Permutational Analysis of Multivariate Dispersions) was conducted to test for homogeneity of multivariate dispersions. Non-significant PERMDISP results (P > 0.05) indicate homogenous dispersion, validating that the differences detected by PERMANOVA are driven by location effects (community composition) rather than dispersion effects.
